  "problem": "If $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{7}{2},$ then what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$",
  "worked_solution": "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{7}{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
